From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 22:39:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] Subscribe to bus before incrementing liveness counter

When a new TUI attached, its footer's "live" indicator stayed at the
stale count until *another* client triggered the next change.

Cause: in event.ts the _incr call (which publishes LiveSessionsChanged
via Bus.publish) ran BEFORE Bus.subscribeAll registered this request as
a subscriber. The publish dispatched to the existing subscriber set,
which did not yet include the just-attaching request. The new TUI
missed its own "you just went live" announcement.

Subsequent events from other clients arrived correctly because by then
the bus subscription was active.

Fix: move Bus.subscribeAll above _incr. The new subscriber is
registered before the publish, so it receives its own announcement and
the footer updates within one event of the SSE handshake.

stop() references heartbeat and unsub via closure; both are still
initialized before stop is invoked (only via the abort listeners wired
up after this block), so the reorder is safe.
---
 packages/opencode/src/server/routes/event.ts | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/opencode/src/server/routes/event.ts b/packages/opencode/src/server/routes/event.ts
index fd9dfe5..abebeae 100644
--- a/packages/opencode/src/server/routes/event.ts
+++ b/packages/opencode/src/server/routes/event.ts
@@ -94,8 +94,6 @@ export const EventRoutes = () =>
         const q = new AsyncQueue<string | null>()
         let done = false

-        if (sessionID) _incr(sessionID)
-
         q.push(
           JSON.stringify({
             type: "server.connected",
@@ -130,6 +128,15 @@ export const EventRoutes = () =>
           }
         })

+        // Hivemind: _incr publishes LiveSessionsChanged via Bus.publish (see
+        // _publishChange above). The publish must happen AFTER the
+        // Bus.subscribeAll above so this request receives its own
+        // "you just went live" event — otherwise the TUI footer that just
+        // attached doesn't update to reflect itself until *another* client
+        // triggers the next change. Reorder is a pure semantic fix; no
+        // behavior change beyond the timing window.
+        if (sessionID) _incr(sessionID)
